# Independent artifact export review

Reviewed new tools/site/artifact.py and test_artifact_export.py on base 3104041, against the previously reviewed selected/payload/recovery boundary and spec15 same-artifact contract. No implementation edits or API/publication operations.

No blocking finding. Reads are bounded before calling selected; no output is opened until all metadata, ZIP, receipt, raw-tar and source validation finishes. The output parent retains production real_directory checks and xb refuses existing paths rather than overwriting them. CLI errors from export return a failed JSON report and nonzero status without including exception text. Fixed own-script import path supports the isolated -I invocation without relying on the caller working directory. Output receipt explicitly keeps publication_verified false.

Independent normal and python -O runs each passed 2 tests, including actual -I CLI subprocess execution, original bytes, existing-output refusal and invalid-input absence. An additional actual Windows junction output-parent probe was rejected before output creation; its resolved target had no new file. Evidence includes raw logs and commands.

This is a local file handoff, not authenticated download, run eligibility, Pages upload or publication authorization. Filesystem write/close errors can leave a partial new output, but cannot return the success receipt; this is not an atomic replace or crash-durability guarantee. Bounded byte reads do not impose a wall-clock deadline on blocking filesystem I/O, and ZIP central-directory memory limits remain the previously documented caller/isolated-host responsibility. No live API or cross-platform run was performed by this review.

Final tools/site/README.md independently reviewed: invocation arguments, output requirements, partial-write behavior, distinct Pages upload identity and caller isolation/eligibility duties match the implementation. Exact snapshots include both Python files and this README.
